      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n, s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &mat[i][j]);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Build integral image using two-pass method:\n\t// First pass: row-wise prefix sums\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<long long>> row_pref(n + 1, std::vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n\tfor (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n\t\tlong long sum = 0;\n\t\tfor (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tsum += mat[i - 1][j - 1];\n\t\t\trow_pref[i][j] = sum;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Second pass: column-wise prefix sums on row_pref to obtain full integral image\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<long long>> pref(n + 1, std::vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n\tfor (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j) {\n\t\tlong long sum = 0;\n\t\tfor (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n\t\t\tsum += row_pref[i][j];\n\t\t\tpref[i][j] = sum;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Search all top-left corners using integral image formula\n\tlong long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n#pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(dynamic,16)\n\tfor (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n\t\t\tlong long sum = pref[i + s][j + s] - pref[i][j + s] - pref[i + s][j] + pref[i][j];\n\t\t\tif (sum > mxSum)\n\t\t\t\tmxSum = sum;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n\treturn 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Use integral image computed via two parallel prefix sum passes (row then column) each with static scheduling, and search all top-left corners using collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(dynamic,16). This demonstrates OpenMP work sharing through parallel for directives on both construction and search phases, reductions via max reduction, explicit dynamic scheduling to balance irregular workload in the search phase (due to varying submatrix sums), and thread granularity via collapsed loops.",
